" Tridactyl in Zen (modules/features/zen). Its own defaults are already Vim's: j/k scroll, f follows a
" link, o opens, t opens in a new tab, d closes, H/L go back and forward, gt/gT switch tabs, / finds,
" : is the command line. In the browser, :help lists every key and :tutor teaches them.
"
" Read at every start; anything changed in the browser with :set or :bind lasts until then.

" Start from the defaults each time, so a line removed here is gone from the browser too.
sanitise tridactyllocal tridactylsync

" Links are followed with the home row.
set hintchars asdfghjkl

set smoothscroll true

" Ctrl+I in a text field opens it in Neovim, in a kitty window; :wq puts the text back.
set editorcmd kitty -e nvim %f

colourscheme dark
